  "title": "Is trust the Achilles’ heel or the force behind agentic AI adoption?",
  "summary": "<ul> <li>A future where artificial intelligence (AI) agents take over everyday tasks is intriguing, but it immediately raises questions of trust. Can we really rely on them? Or can it be that they&rsquo;re more trustworthy than us?</li> <li>If we do hand over tasks to agentic AI, trust mechanisms must exist, along with clear trust layers around these agents. Let&rsquo;s reflect on these together.</li> </ul>",
